---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<Page
  title="Privacy Policy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="June 15, 2026"
  description="How Em Dash Remover handles your data - your text never leaves your browser. Full disclosure of cookies, analytics, and advertising."
>
  <p>
    <strong>The short version:</strong> the text you paste into Em Dash Remover never
    leaves your device. All text processing happens locally in your browser. We
    don't upload, store, or log the content you clean. You can verify this: open your
    browser's developer tools, go to the Network tab, and watch - there are no
    requests while you clean text. The tool even works with your internet turned off.
  </p>
  <p>
    This page explains, in full, what limited data the website itself involves
    (cookies, analytics, and advertising) so you can make informed choices.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Text you process</h2>
  <p>
    Any text you enter into the cleaner is processed entirely client-side (in your
    browser). It is never transmitted to us or any third party, and we keep no copies.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Local storage</h2>
  <p>
    We use your browser's local storage to remember your preferences - your chosen
    cleanup options, theme, and cookie-consent choice - so the tool behaves the way
    you like next time. This data stays on your device and is never sent to us. You
    can clear it any time via your browser settings.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The core tool does not require cookies to function. Cookies on this site come
    from two optional sources, both of which depend on your consent: analytics and
    advertising (described below). When you first visit, you can <strong>Accept</strong>
    or <strong>Decline</strong> these via our cookie banner, and change your choice
    anytime through the <a href="#" data-cookie-settings>Cookie settings</a> link in
    the footer. See our <a href="/cookies">Cookie Policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Advertising &amp; Google AdSense</h2>
  <p>
    We may display advertising served by Google AdSense to keep this tool free.
    The following disclosures are required by Google:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a
      user's prior visits to this website or other websites.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads
      to you based on your visit to this and/or other sites on the Internet.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
      <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can also opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalised
      advertising at
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">aboutads.info</a>
      and
      <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">optout.networkadvertising.org</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For visitors in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and Switzerland,
    we use a Google-certified consent management platform and Google Consent Mode so
    that personalised advertising and analytics cookies are only used after you give
    consent. Until you consent, ads (if shown) are limited and non-personalised.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We may use privacy-friendly analytics to understand aggregate traffic (such as
    page views and referrers). These tools do not receive the text you process. Where
    analytics rely on cookies, they are loaded only after you consent.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights (GDPR / UK GDPR)</h2>
  <p>
    If you are in the EEA or UK, you have the right to access, correct, or delete your
    personal data, to object to or restrict its processing, and to data portability.
    Because we don't collect or store your text or build user profiles ourselves,
    most personal data on this site is handled by the third parties named above under
    their own policies (see
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google's Privacy Policy</a>).
    You can exercise consent choices at any time via the cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights (CCPA / California)</h2>
  <p>
    If you are a California resident, you have the right to know what personal
    information is collected, to request deletion, and to opt out of the "sale" or
    "sharing" of personal information. We do not sell your personal information. You
    can limit advertising cookies using the opt-out links in section 4 or by
    declining via our cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
    personal information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on
    this page with an updated revision date.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about your privacy? Email us at
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or use our
    <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="text-sm muted">
    This document is a general template and does not constitute legal advice. Please
    have it reviewed by a qualified professional for your jurisdiction.
  </p>
</Page>
